            {
              "id": "CVE-2025-60876-busybox",
              "name": "ApkMatcherCpeMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2025-60876 medium vulnerability for busybox package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "BusyBox wget thru 1.3.7 accepted raw CR (0x0D)/LF (0x0A) and other C0 control bytes in the HTTP request-target (path/query), allowing the request line to be split and attacker-controlled headers to be injected. To preserve the HTTP/1.1 request-line shape METHOD SP request-target SP HTTP/1.1, a raw space (0x20) in the request-target must also be rejected (clients should use %20)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-60876",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2025-60876\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: busybox\nVersion: 1.37.0-r30\nFix Version: \nType: apk\nLocation: /lib/apk/db/installed\nData Namespace: nvd:cpe\nLink: [CVE-2025-60876](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-60876)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2025-60876**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | busybox  | 1.37.0-r30  |   | apk  | /lib/apk/db/installed  | nvd:cpe  | [CVE-2025-60876](https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-60876)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:apk/alpine/busybox@1.37.0-r30?arch=aarch64&distro=alpine-3.23.4"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.5"
              }
            },
